// Syllabus — Distributed Computing (curated course; see collection.js for references)
//
// Sources consulted (Oct 2026):
//   Lynch, Distributed Algorithms (1996) — full contents with section numbers (book PDF front matter):
//     https://groups.csail.mit.edu/tds/distalgs.html
//   Attiya & Welch, Distributed Computing, 2nd ed. — chapter list (Library of Congress TOC):
//     http://catdir.loc.gov/catdir/toc/wiley041/2004040728.html
//   Cambridge Part IB Concurrent and Distributed Systems (Kleppmann): system models, clocks,
//     broadcast, replication, Raft, linearizability, ABD, CAP, CRDTs, Spanner:
//     https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/teaching/2324/ConcDisSys/
//   MIT 6.5840/6.824 Distributed Systems schedule (Paxos, Raft, linearizability, Spanner, chain
//     replication, Bitcoin, PBFT): https://pdos.csail.mit.edu/6.824/schedule.html
// Lynch is cited by section, Attiya–Welch by chapter. Systems results that post-date both books
// or lie outside them — Raft, chain replication, PBFT, Nakamoto consensus, CAP/PACELC, CRDTs,
// Dynamo quorums, gossip, consistent hashing, Chord, TrueTime, Cole–Vishkin, self-stabilization —
// are referred to the nearest chapter. Deliberately omitted: MapReduce and data-parallel
// frameworks, distributed transactions beyond commit protocols, and population protocols.
// Landmark papers (kind 'Paper', Oct 2026): each citation was checked against its Crossref record (api.crossref.org/works/<doi>)
// or, without a DOI, against the cited record (NASA NTRS, Google Patents, Euler Archive, Smithsonian Libraries).
